    {
      "id": "claim_5165525b2c374c5dae93b358a4366024",
      "statement": "client.ts enforces a token barrier: authPermanentFailure short-circuits execute/executeRaw with a synchronous throw, and GET requests without a JS access_token await awaitAuthReady() (the authStore-registered restoreToken provider, capped at 10 seconds) before web mode throws UNAUTHORIZED; the gate also covers the native branch because the Java-heap token is produced asynchronously by the OAuth exchange, while POST requests are intentionally not gated.",
      "evidence": [
